WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.500
The kit checks the register in two ways.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.427
The first is the register check,
rules W R oh one to oh nine,

3
00:00:06.427 --> 00:00:10.013
which test the register's
shape before you trust it.

4
00:00:10.013 --> 00:00:13.412
A row must name a single
writer and appear only once.

5
00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:16.287
Every writer and backstop must be defined.

6
00:00:16.287 --> 00:00:18.682
A writer with no
identities gets a warning,

7
00:00:18.682 --> 00:00:21.350
because the scan couldn't
attribute its writes.

8
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:25.062
Every required account-state
transition, created,

9
00:00:25.062 --> 00:00:28.863
enabled, disabled, re-enabled
and deleted, needs a row.

10
00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:32.200
Deletion must never be written
by inbound provisioning.

11
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.575
A backstop can't be the writer itself.

12
00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:38.525
Two rows for the same audited change
can't name different writers.

13
00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:42.875
And the register should be recorded as
signed, with a versioned scope filter.

14
00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:46.394
Every tool in the kit
uses the same exit codes:

15
00:00:46.394 --> 00:00:51.220
zero when clean, two for findings
or warnings, one for an error.
